# Automation And Docs

- Keep CI/helper scripts dependency-light; match existing patterns built around the standard library, `pathlib`, and `subprocess.run`.
- Only edit workflows when the task requires it, and keep actions pinned to stable major versions.
- Keep docs and README commands aligned with real scripts and workflows; avoid reintroducing stale workflow names.
- Use `requirements-docs.txt` and `mkdocs.yml` as the source of truth for docs build behavior.
- When changing `wow_interface_sync.py`, its fixtures, or parser behavior, update or run `tests/test_wow_interface_sync.py`.
- When changing README Interface badge formatting or `blizzard_api.py` display conversion, update or run `tests/test_interface_badge.py`.
